  "eps_text": "GAAP EPS from continuing operations loss of $2.56 included $2.96 of net significant and/or non-recurring charges and acquisition accounting adjustments, of which $2.34 related to the current economic environment (COVID-19; $2.13 Collins goodwill and intangibles impairment), $0.28 acquisition accounting adjustments and $0.21 restructuring.",
  "guidance": "No numeric outlook in the release. Text: \"Looking ahead, we expect the pressures in commercial aerospace to persist as OEM production levels and aftermarket activity remain low.\" (2020 cost-reduction and cash-conservation targets reported as achieved ~$600 million / ~$1 billion in Q2.)",
  "definitions": "Adjusted net sales represents consolidated net sales from continuing operations (a GAAP measure), excluding other significant items. Adjusted operating profit (loss) represents income from continuing operations (a GAAP measure), excluding restructuring costs, acquisition accounting adjustments and other significant items. Adjusted net income / EPS: net income / diluted EPS from continuing operations excluding restructuring costs, acquisition accounting adjustments and other significant items. Adjusted diluted weighted average shares outstanding includes stock awards that were anti-dilutive because of the reported net loss. Adjusted effective tax rate excludes the tax effect of restructuring costs, acquisition accounting adjustments and other significant items. Acquisition accounting adjustments include amortization and impairment of acquired intangible assets, amortization of the PP&E fair value adjustment and amortization of acquired customer contractual obligations (definition revised with the Raytheon Merger; all periods presented reflect the change). Free cash flow represents cash flow from operations (continuing operations) less capital expenditures."
 },
